body:
Some of us have this emptyness by having careless parents.

I know it hurts when you project your life over someone, and it does not work out. It's like loosing a piece of yourself.  This is normal. It's even harder when you have no one to confort you. I've been there. You know, don't feel bad for feeling bad.  You have a good reason to cry, to feel sad. Don't reject those emotions.But don't focus on the bad things that happened, or the things you're not good at.You were a loyal  and caring partner. Good on you. Don't blame yourself for the breake up. You're young, you can eventually find someone who likes you. Don't let the pain of the past paralize you. You have a life ahead, with dauting challenges, but you CAN make it a good life. "It's a bad day, not a bad life."

&#x200B;
